Tenko Linux first-boot root password policy
==============================================

Tenko ships /etc/shadow with the root account locked.  On the first boot
of such an image, tenko-firstboot-root-password.service runs on tty1
before getty@tty1.service and asks for a new root password using passwd(1).
The prompt is visible on the physical/VGA console (tty1).  After the
password is set, /var/lib/tenko/firstboot-root-password.done is written
and the service never prompts again.

Images that already have a root password are not prompted.  For example,
the QEMU test image sets root/root; on boot the service detects a usable
password, records the marker, and exits immediately.

Serial console only (no VGA/tty1)
---------------------------------
The automated prompt is bound to tty1, so a machine booted only with
console=ttyS0 does not show it.  Log in as root on the serial console and
set the password manually:

    passwd root

The service will then detect a usable password on the next boot and skip
the prompt.  If boot is blocked waiting for the tty1 prompt, boot with

    systemd.mask=tenko-firstboot-root-password.service

log in on the serial console, run "passwd root", then reboot normally.

The same result can be achieved non-interactively from a serial console:

    printf 'new-password\nnew-password\n' | passwd root

Security note: choose a password that is not shipped in the image or in
build scripts.  The test images use a throwaway root/root password and are
not intended for deployment.
